    "field": "Integrated assessment of climate change",
    "problem": "Assessing the costs and uncertainties of achieving climate targets is challenging because individual models only capture limited parametric uncertainty, failing to integrate the full uncertainty range from climate science, emissions reductions, and socio-economic assumptions found across the broader scientific literature.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a metamodel that synthesizes key relationships from climate and integrated assessment models to assess the emissions budgets, mitigation costs, and sources of uncertainty for achieving global temperature targets.",
    "task": "The task is to construct a metamodel from climate and integrated assessment models to assess the emissions budgets, costs, and sources of uncertainty associated with achieving specific global temperature targets, such as 1.5 \u00b0C and 2 \u00b0C.",
