    "obs_and_metrics": [],
    "innovation": "This paper constructs a metamodel that synthesizes the full uncertainty range from climate and integrated assessment literature to quantify the costs of climate targets and identify that economic uncertainty, rather than climate system uncertainty, dominates for achieving the Paris Agreement goals.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Earth system model (ESM)",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "transient climate response to cumulative CO2 emissions (TCRE)",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The first element is the transient climate response to cumulative CO2 emissions (TCRE), which shows the relationship between cumulative CO2 emissions and temperature change (Fig. 1a). This emergent property of Earth system model (ESM) simulations implies that each temperature target can be translated relatively easily into a carbon budget, given a specific choice of how to deal with uncertainty\u00b9\u2074.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "models used in the fifth round of the Coupled Model Intercomparison Project (CMIP5)",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "BELONGS_TO_MIP_ERA",
            "target_entity_instance": "CMIP5",
            "target_entity_type": "MIPEra",
            "paragraph": "Similar to the IPCC SR1.5 budgets, the climate feedbacks not covered in the models used in the fifth round of the Coupled Model Intercomparison Project (CMIP5) could lead to a reduction of 100 GtCO2 in the budgets mentioned here \u00b9\u2078.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MAGICC climate model",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "long-term temperature increases",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "While this database only reports the forcing for CO2 and non-CO\u2082 separately, the forcing can be converted to long-term temperature increases using the relation as used in the MAGICC climate model32.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "integrated assessment models",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "PRODUCES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "abatement costs",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Finally, the mitigation costs are also obtained from the SSP database. In the literature, various costs metrics are used, partly because the models can only express certain cost types. Three costs measures often used (and included in the SSP database) are: (1) consumption losses, (2) abatement costs often measured as the area under an abatement curve\u2014and (3) carbon prices.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        }
    ],
